# What alacritty.lua needs from outside Hammerspoon, declared beside the only file that
# knows this tool exists. Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason.
# See Olm's lib/deps.lua for the kinds and for how these files are found.
#
# Alacritty carries no AppleScript dictionary, so a fresh attach is opened through its own
# -e flag instead, reached through open, the one door from Hammerspoon to a bundle's own
# argv. Optional, since the whole tool degrades to whichever other terminals are actually
# installed rather than refusing to open over one missing backend, and open ships with
# macOS regardless.
open | system | /usr/bin/open | optional | launching Alacritty with the flag that starts it attached to a session
